# Virtua Cop
#
# GAME SYSTEM / COUNTRY: JPN to USA.
# The service button moves the cursor; the test button selects a row and
# cycles the value on it.
#
# Changing COUNTRY makes the game re-initialise its text for the new region,
# and inputs are dropped while that happens -- the waits after each value
# change are longer for that reason. The cursor also skips the HUMAN TYPE and
# RELOAD TYPE rows, so EXIT is four moves below COUNTRY, not six.
#
# Drives the game's own test menu, because that is the only supported way to
# change a setting these boards keep in battery-backed RAM. Regenerate with:
#
#     tools/make-defaults.sh vcop
run 700
testmenu 60
run 150
# BOOKKEEPING, then GAME SYSTEM.
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 15
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 15
input in0 0xFB
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 40
# The cursor enters the page on EXIT: ADVERTISE SOUND, then COUNTRY.
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 15
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 15
# JPN to EXP, then EXP to USA.
input in0 0xFB
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 120
input in0 0xFB
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 120
# CABINET, DIFFICULTY, LIFE, EXIT.
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
# Back to the main menu, which returns with the cursor on GAME SYSTEM.
input in0 0xFB
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 120
# COIN ASSIGNMENT through BACKUP RAM CLEAR, then EXIT.
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
input in0 0xF7
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 60
# Leaving the menus properly is what makes the game commit the change to
# backup RAM.
input in0 0xFB
run 5
input in0 0xFF
run 120
run 400
nvram defaults
